# Linear workflow (automatic)

Project: **Nexuses Unified Portal** · Team: **Nexuses** · MCP: `plugin-linear-linear`

## When starting a feature / non-trivial change

1. Create a Linear issue with `save_issue`:
   - `team`: `Nexuses`
   - `project`: `Nexuses Unified Portal`
   - `state`: `In Progress`
   - `milestone`: `Local — not pushed` (create milestone if missing)
   - Clear title + short description of scope/files
2. Do the work. Prefer mentioning the issue id (e.g. `NEX-270`) in commit messages when committing.

## After a successful `git push` to remote

1. Move related In Progress issues for this work to **Done** (`state: Done`).
2. Set `milestone` to **Shipped on master** (create/update if needed).
3. Append a short note to the issue description: commit hash + that it was pushed to `master`.
4. Update the **Shipped on master** and **Local — not pushed** milestone descriptions so Done vs WIP stay accurate.
5. Lightly refresh the project description/summary if the shipped feature set changed.

## Rules of thumb

- Small typo-only fixes: skip new issues.
- Already-tracked work: update the existing issue instead of duplicating.
- Never invent Linear status — use real statuses: Todo / In Progress / Done.
- If Linear MCP is unavailable, say so once and continue coding; retry Linear when auth is back.
